    "causalModel": {
      "founding": "The assembly designated this Hist for tapping and issued one licence against it: one stage, one season, one tree. The stage stands where the crew could raise it without cutting into the root flare.",
      "siteAdvantages": "A firm terrace 3.1 m above the water table, 16 m from a channel deep enough (0.9 m) to pole a loaded canoe, under closed canopy that hides the camp from the land side until the last thirty metres.",
      "occupantsMotive": "A tapper and two crew whose licence is their livelihood. They keep the stage correct and police poachers themselves, because a district that cannot police itself loses its licences.",
      "pressures": "The licence is renewed annually and the objection comes most reliably from the tribe whose tree carried the stage last year. Night landings at the same channel are not the crew's work and are not stopped by them either.",
      "wouldChangeIf": "A licence revoked would empty the stage within a season and make the same channel a poacher's road."
    },
