          "why": "Slope 1.12 deg, 3.09 m above the water table, flood band 0, 16.3 m to a shore whose channel measures 0.9 m deep 16 m to the NNW (bearing 330) — the only water within 250 m that a loaded canoe can be poled along. Height delta across a 20 m box is 3.9 m but only 1.6 m across the 18 m the pieces actually occupy. Canopy closure 0.92, open-space radius p50 6.7 m, so the camp is unseen from the land side until roughly 30 m. Route 615 m to the Helstrom-Blackrose road, reached by one track from the south-east; every other approach is water, reed margin or unbroken jungle."
